<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Partizaner-Marsh (Shmerke Kaczerginski)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1943</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new Yiddish words based on the text</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Yiddish version (Leyb Rozental, Vilna Ghetto)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Song of the United Front (Charlie Haden, Liberation Music Orchestra)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Warum geht es mir so dreckig? (Ton Steine Scherben)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1971</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover, slightly altered</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Free-jazz version (Brötzmann/Van Hove/Bennink)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1973</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hannes Wader singt Arbeiterlieder (Hannes Wader)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1977</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li></ul></section>
